  "summary": "The drawing implements the architecture the specification describes: a CM4 carrier (Module2A/2B) with two MCP2515 SPI CAN controllers clocked by 16 MHz crystals (Y4/Y5) through isolated CAN transceivers (U20/U21) to the CAN connectors, an LTC4412xS6 + P-channel MOSFET (U28/Q10) ideal-diode USB path, SN74LVC1G07 buffers wired as /OE sinks for the e-stop/indicator chain, a WS2812B string behind a TXS0101 level shifter, and ISL54222AIUZ analog switches for USB/serial muxing. Reference designators differ from the spec's reference design (e.g. LTC4412 is U28 not U6, CAN controllers are U7/U9 not U8/U9, CAN connectors are J10/J29 not J2/J13, the 7-seg driver occupies U35/U36), but this is expected for a different build of the same board and the functions themselves are present and correctly wired. Every apparent mismatch is a documented known-issue/limitation in the spec (RS-485-vs-CAN README discrepancy, 16 MHz crystal requirement which the drawing satisfies, C5 footprint, 'USB diode doesn't work' resolved by the LTC4412, GLOBAL_EN having no sequencing IC, 'are any switches backwards'), none of which are anomalies. No deviation that would make the board behave differently from the intended design is supported by the drawing."
}

